Chapter: SmpQuantum
  cites Kernel chapter Hpet

 codex-vm models the LAPIC bus at 100 MHz, so a 10 ms quantum at divide-by-16
 is a count of 62,500; 56,250 to 68,750 is ten per cent either side. The bed
 hands a compute-bound AP its tick only when its kick thread cancels the run,
 once per core 0 PIT period. What it can show is that the APs program the
 measured count: the 160 ms count the literal gave took a tick on every third
 55 ms kick, 18 a second, and 36 separates that from the calibrated count.
 Cell 28672 is core 0's tick count, and codex-vm paces core 0 from the reload
 the kernel programs, 11,932, about 100 a second; a codex-vm pacing at a fixed
 55 ms reads 18, and 60 to 130 separates them.
 Cell 36216 counts every tick an AP takes while running a process, and
 cell 36352 holds the count the boot processor measured. The spinners stop on
 cell 36360, which nothing else in the tree or codex-vm uses, because codex-vm
 answers an AP's HPET read with 0: only the boot processor can time the window.

Section: Body

  spin-until-stop : Integer -> Integer
  spin-until-stop (acc) = if atomic-load 36360 /= 0 then acc else spin-until-stop (acc + 1)

  wait-until : Integer -> Integer
  wait-until (deadline) = if hpet-ticks >= deadline then 0 else wait-until deadline

  opening : [Console, Concurrent] Nothing = act
    let started = hpet-start
    in let rate = hpet-ticks-per-second
    in let t0 = hpet-ticks
    in let go = atomic-store 36360 0
    in act
      a <- process-spawn (\x -> spin-until-stop x)
      b <- process-spawn (\x -> spin-until-stop x)
      c <- process-spawn (\x -> spin-until-stop x)
      d <- process-spawn (\x -> spin-until-stop x)
      e <- process-spawn (\x -> spin-until-stop x)
      f <- process-spawn (\x -> spin-until-stop x)
      let w1 = wait-until (t0 + rate)
      in let c1 = atomic-load 36216
      in let p1 = atomic-load 28672
      in let w2 = wait-until (t0 + 2 * rate)
      in let c2 = atomic-load 36216
      in let p2 = atomic-load 28672
      in let n = c2 - c1
      in let k = atomic-load 36352
      in let stop = atomic-store 36360 1
      in act
        wa <- process-wait a
        wb <- process-wait b
        wc <- process-wait c
        wd <- process-wait d
        we <- process-wait e
        wf <- process-wait f
        print-line-uni (if k > 0 & k /= 1000000 then "the count was calibrated" else "THE COUNT WAS NOT CALIBRATED: " & show k)
        print-line-uni (if k >= 56250 & k <= 68750 then "the count is 10 ms at the modelled bus" else "THE COUNT IS " & show k)
        print-line-uni (if n >= 36 then "ap ticks outpace the 160 ms count" else "AP TICKS " & show n & " IN ONE SECOND")
        print-line-uni (if p2 - p1 >= 60 & p2 - p1 <= 130 then "the tick count is core 0's clock" else "TICK COUNT ADVANCED " & show (p2 - p1) & " IN ONE SECOND")
      end
    end
  end
